    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d875">

                <pb facs="0943" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.622a/214</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Laughlin</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-08-30T16:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">August 30, 1916, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received 5.30 p. m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4795. For Ambassador Page: Your August 23,
                    4 p. m. Lord Grey informs me that the
                    Colonial Office is now handling the <hi rendition="#italic">China</hi> case and
                    that they have telegraphed the Governor General of Australia instructions to
                    convey the prisoners to Shanghai in a British ship.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Laughlin</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
